      "measure.moments_coords": "Coordinate inputs are owning N-by-2 point clouds prepared outside timing from the first 2*N seeded gray values; size denotes points and dtype is the actual coordinate dtype. NumPy tuple/center/cast/power preparation remains explicit; ordinary finite real typed products and reduction are owned C++. K1, complex and exceptional domains use NumPy primitives without reduction credit. Genuine reference monomials are captured outside timing for the frozen 2*gamma_(N+D)*S policy.",
